From: ios-milanf-port (desk phase, 2026-10-24)
Subject: [PATCH] MILANF: build the console crash report on milanf too

bsd/conf/files lists bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c as 'standard', so it is
compiled for every board, and it calls sweet_sample_task(). That
function, together with the rest of the console crash reporter, is
defined in osfmk/kern/exception.c behind
  #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
so the MILANF link fails with exactly one undefined symbol:

  _sweet_sample_task, referenced from _sweet_sample_proc in sweet_sample.o

The reporter is not board-specific: it prints user registers, a
frame-pointer backtrace, the shared-cache slide, the Mach-O header and
(for processes named in the sweetscan boot-arg) printable heap strings.
Milanf is the same kind of device - a phone with no way to get logs off
it - so the guard covers both boards. The caller in bsd/kern/kern_exit.c
carries its own guard and stays as it is.

diff --git a/osfmk/kern/exception.c b/osfmk/kern/exception.c
index a20a764..d6e11a3 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/exception.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/exception.c
@@ -820,7 +820,7 @@ exception_triage(
 	return exception_triage_thread(exception, code, codeCnt, thread);
 }
 
-#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
 #include <vm/vm_shared_region.h>
 #include <arm/thread.h>
 
